# Spacing, margins, and grid layout

All min apps (WatchedIt, PodLink, YourTube, Cyclismo) share a unified spacing system. The canonical source is `MinSpacing` in `packages/design-system/swift/Sources/MinAppKit/Tokens/MinSpacing.swift` and `spacing.js`.

## Spacing scale

| Token | Points | Use |
|-------|--------|-----|
| `xs`  | 4      | Tight internal gaps |
| `sm`  | 8      | Button gaps, small internal padding |
| `md`  | 12     | Inter-component spacing |
| `lg`  | 16     | **Toolbar/button/nav edge inset**, grid gutters |
| `xl`  | 24     | **Screen content margins** (= `screenHorizontalPadding`) |
| `xxl` | 32     | Section spacing |

## Screen content margins (`xl` / 24pt)

All scroll content, detail views, onboarding panels, list rows, and page-level elements use `screenHorizontalPadding` (24pt) from the screen edge.

```swift
// Swift — screen content
.padding(.horizontal, DesignSystem.Spacing.screenHorizontalPadding)
// or
.padding(.horizontal, MinSpacing.screenHorizontalPadding)
```

```css
/* CSS — use the variable, not a literal */
padding-left: var(--min-page-margin-left);   /* 24px */
padding-right: var(--min-page-margin-right);  /* 24px */
```

## Floating controls inset (`lg` / 16pt)

Floating toolbars, search bars, account buttons, layout-toggle FABs, and top safe-area controls sit at `lg` (16pt) — **8pt inside the screen edge** from the content margin. This creates a subtle visual break where chrome extends past content.

```swift
// Floating bottom toolbar
.padding(.horizontal, DesignSystem.Spacing.lg)

// Top controls (account button bar)
.padding(.horizontal, MinSpacing.lg)

// Overlay FABs (leading/trailing)
.padding(.leading, DesignSystem.Spacing.lg)
.padding(.trailing, DesignSystem.Spacing.lg)
```

### Banned patterns for toolbar/control edge insets

```swift
.padding(.horizontal, DesignSystem.Spacing.screenHorizontalPadding) // too far in
.padding(.horizontal, DesignSystem.Spacing.sm)                       // too far out
.padding(.horizontal, DesignSystem.Spacing.md + DesignSystem.Spacing.xs) // legacy 16pt
```

## 2-column grid (PodLink & YourTube)

Both pod min and vid min use an identical 2-column flexible grid:

```swift
private let gridColumns = [
    GridItem(.flexible(), spacing: DesignSystem.Spacing.lg),
    GridItem(.flexible(), spacing: DesignSystem.Spacing.lg)
]

LazyVGrid(columns: gridColumns, spacing: DesignSystem.Spacing.lg) { ... }
    .padding(.horizontal, DesignSystem.Spacing.screenHorizontalPadding) // xl outer margin
```

Key rules:
- **Exactly 2 `.flexible()` columns** — never `.adaptive()` which breaks with wider margins
- **`lg` (16pt) gutter** between columns and between rows — both axes match
- **No fixed-width frames** on grid items — artwork uses `.aspectRatio(1, contentMode: .fit)` to fill the column
- **`xl` (24pt) outer margin** on the grid container

### Banned grid patterns

```swift
GridItem(.adaptive(minimum: 170), spacing: 12)    // breaks column count
.frame(width: artworkSize, height: artworkSize)    // prevents fluid fill
GridItem(.flexible(), spacing: DesignSystem.Spacing.xl) // gutter too wide
```

## Mobile breakpoints

| Platform | Breakpoint | Regular margins | Mobile margins |
|----------|-----------|----------------|---------------|
| CSS      | 767px     | 24px           | 16px          |
| iOS      | compact `horizontalSizeClass` | 24pt | 16pt |
| Android  | 600dp     | 24dp           | 16dp          |
